// ## 9. How agent decides relevant documents

// The agent should **not directly decide from all documents**.

// Correct method:

// ```text
// 1. Admin/client tags document during upload
// 2. System stores document_type and allowed_agents
// 3. Document router filters by allowed document types
// 4. Vector search retrieves top relevant chunks
// 5. Sub-agent uses only those chunks
// ```

// So relevance is decided by:

// ```text
// Document metadata filter + semantic search + agent policy
// ```

// Not by the LLM alone.

// ---

// ## Final rule

// For professional production design:

// ```text
// Sub-agent should never see all company documents.
// Sub-agent should receive only relevant document chunks.
// Every decision must include evidence.
// If evidence is missing or weak, route to human approval.
// ```
